      "group_id": "PG01",
      "brief": "Create a visually striking public-awareness poster for a wildfire prevention campaign. The poster should communicate that a single careless action can threaten an entire mountain landscape. Develop a memorable central visual involving a forested mountain, smoke, fire, or another meaningful representation of wildfire risk. The image may be realistic, illustrative, symbolic, or abstract, but it should feel emotionally immediate and specific to the subject. Required text: ONE SPARK IS ENOUGH; Check conditions. Extinguish completely. Protect the wild.; National Forest Safety Initiative. The poster should feel urgent without becoming sensational, graphic, or visually chaotic. It must work as a compelling campaign image when seen from a distance, while keeping every required line readable. Do not design a dashboard, webpage, collection of cards, or informational interface. Create one unified poster composition.",
