      "group_id": "PG05",
      "brief": "Create an evocative theatrical poster for an independent film about memory, distance, and a slowly disappearing hometown. Develop a central visual suggesting a coastal town, an empty road, fading architecture, a distant human presence, or another image that conveys the uncertainty of remembering a place. The poster should imply a story without literally illustrating every narrative detail. Required text: WHERE THE HOUSES END; A film by Mara Venn; Some places disappear twice.; In selected theatres this winter. The result should feel cinematic, emotionally restrained, and visually specific to this film. Avoid generic streaming thumbnails, actor-credit grids, fake review quotes, and conventional template treatments. Do not design a webpage, collection of panels, or informational interface. Create one unified theatrical poster composition.",
